ATTRIBUTION — PRIOR ART

This project is an independent implementation of design ideas first published in:

    Mainplane — https://github.com/mainplane-ai/mainplane
    Author: @Alezander9 and the Mainplane contributors
    License: MIT

Ideas attributed to Mainplane (see docs/prior-art.md for the source-level mapping):

  * Append-only ".state" record files (JSON header line + raw body of exactly len bytes,
    never escaped) as the single source of truth for an agent session.
  * Deterministic rebuild of API context from time-ordered records, with results placed
    directly after the step that produced them and unclosed blocks dropped.
  * Agents as durable identities over a chain of sessions, with per-session prompt snapshots
    and instructions that hot-reload into the live session.
  * "cold_limit" rollover: start a new session when the prompt cache is cold and the session
    is past a token budget, rather than only at a hard context limit.
  * Handoff: the new session is told where the old session's log lives and retrieves the
    context it needs.
  * A deliberately restricted tool surface, with skill files as the capability extension
    point.

No source code from Mainplane is incorporated into this project. Mainplane is written in Go;
this project is original Python built on Hermes Agent's public plugin API. Both projects are
licensed under the MIT License; a copy of the MIT terms is in LICENSE for this project's own
code.

"Mainplane" is used here only as a descriptive nod and as an internal session tag value; no
affiliation, endorsement, sponsorship or trademark claim is implied. The tag value is a local
implementation detail and may be renamed.

